 "note": "LIFE-865: who may call the two LIFE OS MCP servers (lifeos/buzz/mcp.py, lifeos.inbox.send_to_jim --mcp). `clients` map one trusted fact (the verified OAuth client, or the OS user of a stdio server) to a client id; a caller-supplied id, header, argument or environment variable is never read. `grants` are authorization_gate.Grant rows seeded only with what each client does today (reads for the two chat clients; no `send_to_jim` grant, because no client has that MCP server configured), each with an expiry; revoke = set `revoked` true. `policy` is the access_policy document they are checked against; its keys are fingerprints of the client ids, not secrets. Credentials are named, never held. Nothing here is live-proven. LIFE-873: `credentials` are scoped `lm1.<id>.<secret>` bearer credentials (Jim, Nov 22 2026, comments 13708): the service holds only the SHA-256 of the secret, never the secret; each names the one client it is and the existing Buzz identity it reads as (null = capabilities only). Read grants only; Personal only; expire 2027-02-22; revoke = set `revoked` true.",
